  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Continuity\n\nA function $f : \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is **continuous at** $x_0$ if for every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there is $\\delta > 0$ such that\n\n$$|x - x_0| < \\delta \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; |f(x) - f(x_0)| < \\varepsilon.$$\n\nRead aloud: *if you want $f(x)$ within $\\varepsilon$ of $f(x_0)$, you can guarantee it by keeping $x$ within $\\delta$ of $x_0$.* The δ depends on both ε **and** $x_0$. When the same δ works for *every* $x_0$, the function is **uniformly continuous**.\n\nThis notebook exposes the difference: pointwise continuity is the weakest useful version, uniform continuity is what you actually need for most theorems (Riemann integrability, the fundamental theorem, exchange of limits...).\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 22,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## A continuous function and its δ-window\n\nTake $f(x) = x^2$ at $x_0 = 1$. To guarantee $|f(x) - 1| < \\varepsilon$, how small must $|x - 1|$ be?\n\nAlgebra: $|x^2 - 1| = |x-1|\\,|x+1| < \\delta(2 + \\delta)$ for $|x-1| < \\delta$. To make this $< \\varepsilon$, take $\\delta = \\min(1, \\varepsilon/3)$ (sufficient).\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f1(x) := x^2$\nx0 : 1.0$ y0 : f1(x0)$ eps : 0.3$\ndelta : min(1.0, eps / 3.0)$\n\nx_grid : np_to_list(np_linspace(0.5, 1.5, 200))$\ny_grid : map(lambda([x], float(f1(x))), x_grid)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"f(x) = x²\",\n  lines(x_grid, y_grid),\n  color=\"red\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"f(x₀) ± ε band\",\n  explicit(y0 + eps, t, 0.5, 1.5),\n  color=\"red\", dash=\"dash\",\n  explicit(y0 - eps, t, 0.5, 1.5),\n  color=\"green\", dash=\"dot\", name=\"x₀ ± δ window\",\n  points([x0 - delta, x0 - delta], [0.0, y0 + 2*eps]),\n  marker_size=10,  /* hack to get a vertical-ish marker */\n  title=\"If x is in the δ-window, f(x) is in the ε-band\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"f(x)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$\nprint(\"ε =\", eps, \"  δ =\", delta)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 23,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "ε = 0.3   δ = 0.09999999999999999"
          ]
        },
        {
