    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Pathological: continuous everywhere, nowhere differentiable\n\nWeierstrass (1872) constructed $W(x) = \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a^n \\cos(b^n \\pi x)$ with $0 < a < 1$, $b$ odd integer, $ab > 1 + 3\\pi/2$. It's continuous (uniform convergence of continuous functions; we'll formalise this in `06-uniform-convergence`) but differentiable nowhere.\n\nTruncate to a finite sum to visualise. The graph is rough at every magnification — a fractal.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "a_w : 0.5$ b_w : 7$ N_terms : 30$\nW(x) := sum(a_w^n * cos((b_w^n) * float(%pi) * x), n, 0, N_terms)$\n\nx_w : np_to_list(np_linspace(0, 1, 1500))$\ny_w : map(lambda([x], float(W(x))), x_w)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"purple\", line_width=1, name=\"W(x) (truncated)\",\n  lines(x_w, y_w),\n  title=\"Weierstrass function — continuous everywhere, differentiable nowhere\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"W(x)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 28,
      "outputs": [
